THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

EmberbirdOS is an independent implementation. Its host and guest source is
written by this project; it is *informed by* the design of other projects but
contains none of their source. The components below are either depended upon,
built alongside this project, or distributed with the guest image, and are
attributed here as their licenses require.

The authoritative long-form analysis is docs/LICENSING.md. A complete,
per-component THIRD_PARTY.md and machine-readable SBOM are generated at image
build time (the guest build runs `m sbom` where the tree supports it); this file
is the human-readable root attribution.

  Android Open Source Project (AOSP)
    License: Apache License 2.0
    The guest platform base. EmberbirdOS's guest-side components (HALs,
    hwcomposer, gralloc bridge, NativeBridge wiring, SystemUI adapters) are
    built against and link into AOSP-derived trees.

  BlissOS / BlissRoms-x86 and the Android-Generic Project (AGP)
    License: AOSP-derived (Apache-2.0 core); bundled kernel and some components
    under GPL-2.0 and other per-component licenses
    The v1 guest base (BlissOS `arcadia-x86`). The guest image is built from a
    pinned manifest (image/manifest/arcadia-x86.pinned.xml) rather than
    redistributed as an opaque blob, so per-component obligations are met by
    publishing the build recipe and manifest. GPL-2.0 components are isolated
    inside the guest image and are not linked into EmberbirdOS's host code.

  AOSP Berberis (binary translation framework)
    License: Apache License 2.0
    Upstream provides a RISC-V to x86_64 translator only. ARM/arm64 translation
    is NOT provided upstream and is an optional, user-supplied layer, never
    bundled - see docs/M1-RUNTIME-ARCHITECTURE.md section 5.

  Mesa, gfxstream (Graphics Streaming Kit), ANGLE, SwiftShader
    Licenses: MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD-style, per component
    The graphics stack on both sides of the VM boundary: the guest ICD and the
    host backend. The SwiftShader software renderer is the current baseline;
    GPU-accelerated gfxstream is the target path behind the GRFX-GATE-01 gate.

  QEMU
    License: GPL-2.0
    The VMM EmberbirdOS invokes. It is an external tool driven over its command
    line and is NOT linked into, or redistributed as part of, EmberbirdOS's
    Apache-2.0 source. Users obtain or bundle it separately, which is what keeps
    the combined-work licensing boundary intact (docs/LICENSING.md).

  bytehook (bhook) and shadowhook
    License: MIT
    Optional guest-side instrumentation and compatibility shims. Not part of the
    production render path.

  OpenSSL 3.x and BoringSSL
    License: Apache License 2.0
    Cryptography used by host and guest components.

  Proprietary translators - libhoudini (Intel), libndk_translation (Google)
    License: Proprietary. NOT DISTRIBUTED BY THIS PROJECT.
    ARM translation is an optional capability a user may install at runtime, in
    the same posture as Google Apps: never in source control, never bundled,
    always user-supplied with an in-product notice.

